# Azure vs AWS - Side-by-Side Comparison

## 1. Why Learn Both Azure and AWS?

**Benefits of Multi-Cloud Knowledge**:
- **Flexibility**: Choose best service for each use case
- **Career Opportunities**: Work with multiple cloud providers
- **Vendor Negotiation**: Better pricing through competition
- **Architecture Decisions**: Make informed choices
- **Vendor-Agnostic Patterns**: Design portable solutions

**Key Principle**: Core concepts are similar; differences are primarily in service names and APIs

---

## 2. Service Mapping

### Infrastructure as Code

| Concept | Azure | AWS |
|---------|-------|-----|
| **IaC Tool** | ARM Templates (JSON) | Terraform (HCL) |
| **State Management** | Azure Resource Manager | Terraform State (S3) |
| **Parameterization** | Parameters in ARM | Variables in Terraform |
| **Modules** | Linked Templates | Terraform Modules |
| **Deployment** | `az deployment group create` | `terraform apply` |

**Key Difference**: Azure uses JSON-based ARM Templates, AWS uses HCL-based Terraform (though Terraform also supports Azure)

---

### Container Orchestration

| Concept | Azure | AWS |
|---------|-------|-----|
| **Managed Kubernetes** | AKS (Azure Kubernetes Service) | EKS (Elastic Kubernetes Service) |
| **Serverless Containers** | Container Apps | Fargate (on EKS) |
| **Container Registry** | Azure Container Registry (ACR) | Amazon ECR |
| **Auto-Scaling** | Built-in | Cluster Autoscaler |
| **Load Balancing** | Azure Load Balancer | AWS Load Balancer |

**Key Difference**: Azure has Container Apps (serverless containers), AWS uses Fargate (serverless containers on EKS)

---

### Serverless Computing

| Concept | Azure | AWS |
|---------|-------|-----|
| **Functions** | Azure Functions | AWS Lambda |
| **Event Triggers** | Event Hubs, Service Bus, HTTP | EventBridge, SQS, API Gateway |
| **Pricing Model** | Consumption Plan (pay-per-use) | Pay-per-request + compute time |
| **Cold Start** | ~1-2 seconds | ~100ms-1s |
| **Max Execution Time** | 10 minutes (Consumption) | 15 minutes |

**Key Difference**: Similar functionality, different trigger mechanisms and pricing models

---

### Data Streaming

| Concept | Azure | AWS |
|---------|-------|-----|
| **Kafka Service** | Event Hubs (Kafka-compatible) | MSK (Managed Streaming for Kafka) |
| **Stream Processing** | Stream Analytics | Kinesis Data Analytics |
| **Event Streaming** | Event Hubs | Kinesis Data Streams |
| **Throughput** | 2-10 TU (auto-inflate) | Based on shards |
| **Retention** | 1-7 days | 1-7 days (Kinesis) |

**Key Difference**: Azure Event Hubs is Kafka-compatible, AWS has separate MSK (Kafka) and Kinesis services

---

### Object Storage

| Concept | Azure | AWS |
|---------|-------|-----|
| **Object Storage** | Blob Storage | S3 (Simple Storage Service) |
| **File Storage** | Azure Files (SMB/NFS) | EFS (Elastic File System) |
| **Queue Storage** | Queue Storage | SQS (Simple Queue Service) |
| **Lifecycle Policies** | Lifecycle Management | Lifecycle Policies |
| **Access Tiers** | Hot, Cool, Archive | Standard, IA, Glacier |

**Key Difference**: Similar concepts, different naming (Blob vs S3, Files vs EFS)

---

### Managed Databases

| Concept | Azure | AWS |
|---------|-------|-----|
| **PostgreSQL** | Azure Database for PostgreSQL | RDS PostgreSQL |
| **MySQL** | Azure Database for MySQL | RDS MySQL |
| **SQL Server** | Azure SQL Database | RDS SQL Server |
| **NoSQL** | Cosmos DB | DynamoDB |
| **High Availability** | Multi-AZ deployment | Multi-AZ deployment |

**Key Difference**: Azure has Cosmos DB (multi-model), AWS has DynamoDB (key-value)

---

### Monitoring & Observability

| Concept | Azure | AWS |
|---------|-------|-----|
| **Application Monitoring** | Application Insights | CloudWatch |
| **Logging** | Log Analytics | CloudWatch Logs |
| **Metrics** | Metrics API | CloudWatch Metrics |
| **Alerting** | Alert Rules | CloudWatch Alarms |
| **Distributed Tracing** | Application Insights | X-Ray |
| **Dashboards** | Azure Dashboards | CloudWatch Dashboards |

**Key Difference**: Azure Application Insights is more integrated, AWS separates CloudWatch and X-Ray

---

### CI/CD

| Concept | Azure | AWS |
|---------|-------|-----|
| **CI/CD Platform** | Azure DevOps | CodePipeline |
| **Source Control** | Azure Repos | CodeCommit |
